# LoanSense — Intelligent Loan Approval Prediction System

## Problem Statement
SecureTrust Bank processes hundreds of loan applications daily
using manual verification — slow, biased and inconsistent.
Good customers get rejected. High-risk ones get approved.

LoanSense predicts loan approval or rejection automatically
using historical applicant data and Machine Learning.

## Dataset
- File: loan_approval_data.csv
- Target: Loan_Approved (1 = Approved, 0 = Rejected)
- 20 features: Credit Score, Income, DTI Ratio, 
  Collateral, Employment, Property Area and more

## Workflow

### Step 1 — Data Exploration
- df.info(), df.describe(), df.sample()
- Checked class balance using pie chart
- Analysed Education Level distribution with bar plot

### Step 2 — Handling Missing Values
- Numerical columns → filled with mean (SimpleImputer)
- Categorical columns → filled with most frequent value

### Step 3 — EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis)
- Income and Credit Score distribution (histplot)
- Outlier detection using boxplots (2x2 grid)
- Credit Score vs Loan Approval (hue based histplot)
- Correlation Heatmap to find strongest predictors

### Step 4 — Encoding
- LabelEncoder → Education_Level, Loan_Approved
- OneHotEncoder (drop=first) → Employment, Marital Status,
  Loan Purpose, Property Area, Gender, Employer Category
- Dropped Applicant_ID (not a feature)

### Step 5 — Train Test Split & Scaling
- 80% training / 20% testing
- StandardScaler applied on both train and test sets

### Step 6 — Model Comparison

| Model | Accuracy |
|-------|----------|
| Logistic Regression | - |
| KNN (n=5, scaled) | - |
| Naive Bayes (GaussianNB) | **86%** ✅ Winner |

All models evaluated on:
Accuracy · Precision · Recall · F1-Score · Confusion Matrix

## Key Finding
Naive Bayes outperformed KNN and Logistic Regression
with 86% accuracy — probabilistic classification works
well when features are largely independent of each other.

## Tech Stack
Python · Pandas · NumPy · Matplotlib · Seaborn · Scikit-learn

